load @term/seed/code/space/metric
  find metric-space

# The discrete metric: the simplest distance, zero from a point to itself and one to every other point, treating a set
# as a scatter of equidistant dots. On the mesh the natural metric is the graph distance (the number of edges in the
# shortest path between two cells), the discrete distance the substrate's geometry measures. The form carries the metric
# space.
form discrete-metric
  link space, like metric-space
